From: "Michael R. Crusoe" <michael.crusoe@fu-berlin.de>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:15:54 +0100
Subject: tests: prepend to PYTHONPATH, don't overwrite it
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/22543
Applied-Upstream: https://github.com/python/mypy/commit/d3eb16b08af1ec6a45253a54ec6ad464589c0724

Without this, on systems that rely on PYTHONPATH manipulation like
EasyBuild / environment modules, then test can fail to find librt:

> ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'librt'

See https://github.com/easybuilders/easybuild-easyconfigs/pull/27501#issuecomment-7105000936

diff -ruN mypy-2.4.1.orig/mypy/test/test_diff_cache.py mypy-2.4.1/mypy/test/test_diff_cache.py
--- mypy-2.4.1.orig/mypy/test/test_diff_cache.py	2026-10-28 17:29:07.376572000 +0100
+++ mypy-2.4.1/mypy/test/test_diff_cache.py	2026-11-24 19:27:14.877247433 +0100
@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@
         src_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp()
         output_file = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), "diff.json")
         env = os.environ.copy()
-        env["PYTHONPATH"] = PREFIX
+        existing = env.get("PYTHONPATH")
+        env["PYTHONPATH"] = PREFIX + (os.pathsep + existing if existing else "")
         try:
             cache1 = os.path.join(src_dir, "cache1")
             cache2 = os.path.join(src_dir, "cache2")
